+#### [Demucs](https://github.com/adefossez/demucs)
+> **Description:** Demucs is best known for music source separation, but podcasters can use it to split stems, remove intrusive music beds, and isolate speech from mixed material. The README and model lineage focus on hybrid waveform and spectrogram separation, which makes it stronger for complex audio than simpler filters. It is not a speech-only tool, yet it is extremely useful when episodes contain music, archival material, or messy mixed tracks. The repo remains one of the standard open source separation references.
+
