+## FAQ
+
+### What are the best open source AI tools for podcasters in 2026?
+For most podcast teams, the strongest open stack is `openai/whisper` or `SYSTRAN/faster-whisper` for transcription, `m-bain/whisperX` or `pyannote/pyannote-audio` for alignment and speaker separation, and `Rikorose/DeepFilterNet` or `resemble-ai/resemble-enhance` for cleanup. If you need generated narration, start with `coqui-ai/TTS`, `myshell-ai/OpenVoice`, or `OHF-Voice/piper1-gpl`.
+
+### Which GitHub repos are best for podcast transcription without SaaS?
+The best no-SaaS options in this list are `openai/whisper`, `ggerganov/whisper.cpp`, `SYSTRAN/faster-whisper`, `m-bain/whisperX`, and `ephes/podcast-transcript`. They all run from public GitHub code and can be integrated into local or self-hosted workflows.
+
+### What is the best open source AI tool for removing podcast background noise?
+`Rikorose/DeepFilterNet` is the most direct denoising choice for spoken audio. `resemble-ai/resemble-enhance` is also strong for voice clarity, while `Audio-AGI/AudioSep` and `adefossez/demucs` are better for more complex separation problems.
+
+### Which open source tools help create speaker-labeled podcast transcripts?
+`m-bain/whisperX`, `pyannote/pyannote-audio`, `wenet-e2e/wespeaker`, and `snakers4/silero-vad` are the key repos here. In practice, many teams combine Whisper-family transcription with pyannote diarization and VAD pre-segmentation.
+
+### Are there good GitHub-only AI voice generators for podcast intros and dubbing?
+Yes. `coqui-ai/TTS`, `myshell-ai/MeloTTS`, `myshell-ai/OpenVoice`, `WhisperSpeech/WhisperSpeech`, `fishaudio/fish-speech`, and `OHF-Voice/piper1-gpl` are the most relevant open repos in this list. Your best pick depends on whether you value quality, speed, multilingual support, or local/offline use.
+
+### Why are there so few repos explicitly built "for podcasters"?
+Because most open source creators publish by technical function, not audience. Direct GitHub searches for "podcaster" produced almost no quality results, so the right way to build this list was to map the real podcast workflow and then verify GitHub repos for each stage.
+
+### Can I build a full self-hosted podcast AI workflow from these repos?
+Yes, with some assembly. A practical stack is VAD (`silero-vad`) -> transcription (`faster-whisper`) -> diarization (`pyannote-audio`) -> cleanup (`DeepFilterNet`) -> show-note or subtitle post-processing (`Subtitle Edit`) -> optional TTS (`piper1-gpl` or `TTS`).
+
