+### Audio Cleanup, Enhancement, and Separation
+
+#### [DeepFilterNet](https://github.com/Rikorose/DeepFilterNet)
+> **Description:** DeepFilterNet is an open source deep learning framework for noise suppression, and it is one of the cleanest answers to the "my remote guest sounds rough" problem. The README focuses on real-time full-band speech enhancement and practical tooling for denoising. In podcasting, that translates to cleaning fan noise, room hum, and weak recording environments before editing or publishing. It is especially useful in remote interview workflows where source quality varies episode to episode.
+
+- **GitHub:** [github.com/Rikorose/DeepFilterNet](https://github.com/Rikorose/DeepFilterNet)
+- **Stars:** 5.5k ⭐
+- **Language:** Rust
+- **License:** MIT
+- **Last Commit:** 2025-12-02
+- **Category:** denoise, enhancement, restoration
+- **Best for:** removing background noise from spoken-word recordings
+
+---
+
+#### [resemble-enhance](https://github.com/resemble-ai/resemble-enhance)
+> **Description:** `resemble-enhance` is an AI-powered speech denoising and enhancement project aimed directly at improving voice quality. Its README positions it as a tool for speech enhancement rather than general music mastering, which is exactly what podcasters need for dialogue-heavy recordings. It can help improve clarity, presence, and perceived polish before final mixdown or transcription. GitHub shows a growing community around the project and a Python-based implementation.
+
+- **GitHub:** [github.com/resemble-ai/resemble-enhance](https://github.com/resemble-ai/resemble-enhance)
