+### Subtitles, Captions, and Transcript Editing
+
+This category is an honest gap. Only a few GitHub repos clearly fit podcast-adjacent subtitle editing well enough to include here, and most strong caption tools are not AI-first.
+
+#### [Subtitle Edit](https://github.com/SubtitleEdit/subtitleedit)
+> **Description:** Subtitle Edit is not a pure AI repo, but it remains one of the most practical companions to AI transcript workflows. The GitHub project supports creating, syncing, cleaning, and converting subtitle files, which matters after Whisper-family tools generate rough captions. Podcasters can use it to refine episode subtitles, social clips, and video podcast assets. It is included here because open source AI transcription usually still needs a human-friendly subtitle editor at the finish line.
+
+- **GitHub:** [github.com/SubtitleEdit/subtitleedit](https://github.com/SubtitleEdit/subtitleedit)
+- **Stars:** 10.7k ⭐
+- **Language:** C#
+- **License:** GPL-3.0
